1
00:00:00,507 --> 00:00:02,507
(Sheldon:)Yes, amusing.

2
00:00:02,676 --> 00:00:06,176
(Sheldon:)Extraordinary intelligence might well
appear extraterrestrial to you...

3
00:00:06,346 --> 00:00:08,516
(Sheldon:)...but let me be more specific.

4
00:00:08,682 --> 00:00:11,722
(Sheldon:)I believe you know why I'm here
in the laundry room.

5
00:00:12,227 --> 00:00:14,397
(Penny:)Better acoustics
for your throat singing?

6
00:00:16,023 --> 00:00:18,693
[VOCALIZING]

7
00:00:22,529 --> 00:00:24,029
(Sheldon(trying it):)It's actually not bad.

8
00:00:25,991 --> 00:00:29,531
(Sheldon(trying it):)But my true purpose in being here
will be revealed...

9
00:00:29,703 --> 00:00:33,793
(Sheldon(trying it):)...in this brief PowerPoint presentation.
Ahem. Lights.

10
00:00:43,008 --> 00:00:44,718
"Why Sheldon Cooper, PhD...

11
00:00:44,885 --> 00:00:47,265
(Sheldon(trying it):)...should go to Switzerland
to see the CERN Super Collider:

12
00:00:47,429 --> 00:00:49,809
(Sheldon(trying it):)A PowerPoint presentation
by Sheldon Cooper, PhD."

13
00:00:51,433 --> 00:00:52,763
(Leonard:)Oh, for God's sakes.

14
00:00:53,769 --> 00:00:58,019
(Sheldon:)Here, we have a highly gifted researcher
in the field of particle physics...

